<title>USA: BP to announce alternative energy investment.</title>
<headline>BP to announce alternative energy investment.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Petroleum Co Plc said its group chief executive John Browne will announce the company's first U.S. investment in an alternative energy source.</p>
<p>The investment would be made solely by BP and the project will be located in the San Francisco Bay area.</p>
<p>&quot;We really can not go any further than saying that,&quot; said BP spokesman Tom Koch.</p>
<p>The company said the announcement will be made Monday, May 19 and will be part of a speech Browne is to give on global climate change and the balance of the world's energy resources.</p>
<p>The announcment will be made at 1200/PDT/1500 EDT/1900 GMT at Stanford University in Palo Alto, California.</p>
</text>
